I read a good part of the "Protection Racket efficiency challenge" and
I'm intrigued by it.  I actually find that the PR is fairly easy to
pull off, and there are even benefits that have not been discussed
yet.

I usually play Wizards ('cause they're awesome!) and one of the
problems an early wizard often has is low Wisdom.  Higher wisdom
grants better Pw regeneration, and more Pw granted per level, so it's
fairly useful to a wizard, and more importantly, is useful to have
high at low character levels!  The easiest way to exercise wisdom is
to (E)ngrave 'Elbereth' - which is a very useful tactic in a (non-
illiterate) PR run.  So, we've got a well-used way to exercise wisdom
(and Constitution, BTW) and a long time spent at low levels in which
to exercise it, so by the time you're ready to jump to level 5 or 6,
you've got higher stats then you did when you started the game.

That sort of behavior - trying to get my wisdom as high as possible at
level 1 - was what set me down the PR path.  As you play like that,
you learn how powerful a tool your pet is, and what to do to avoid
monsters, etc, and when I first tried the PR...well, I think I died,
but the 2nd time, I think I made it.  Now, I'm going to see if I can
pull off (at least part of) the challenge on NAO (I'm on run 4 now,
lilmouse).

ANYWAY, part 2 of this post:

I think the idea that you've got to get 7 points of protection to
successfully run the "PR" is absurd; the PR is not set in stone -
survival takes precedence over those points of protection, always.
Part of the joy of the PR is that it's darn easy to abort; kill 1 or 2
monsters, and you'll be well on your way to higher levels.  Playing
this challenge in my 4th game, I nearly died b/c I was stupid and
unwilling to give up that 7th point - all sorts of risky behavior!  I
would have called the PR a success at 5 points, myself.

SO, my 4th PR run:

I have an orcish barbarian, and found the mines fairly easily, but
they were dark - boo.  Still, I made good headway, and then found a
pickax dropped by some pet-kill.  Remembering the discussion I read
about the PR, I dug down a level.  I must say, that's darn risky!  If
you end up in the middle of a room of G lords and h's with bows and
arrows, life is tough!!  You don't know where safety is, your pet is
busy eating, and there are LOTS of nasties out there, throwing daggers
and shooting arrows...very unpleasant.  I would have had to start
killing them except I found a lucky /oDigging on 1st mine level, which
let me circle around the big open area, back behind my pet.

Even in a dark mine, I think I prefer the slow, cautious, 'clear the
level' strategy.  You've always got a relatively safe area behind you,
and at the right speed (i.e., cautious), your pet will generally be
near max hp.  Infravision (as orcs have) makes this even safer, as you
can see what's coming in open areas.

That said, I made it to minetown (caverns level).  And that's when I
made several tactical blunders.

1st, I tried credit cloning in Izchak's shop while I was almost
burdened with stuff to sell in the general store.

2nd, and much worse, I walked away from my gold in Izchak's shop to
sell the stupid stuff - don't know what I was thinking.  This meant
that I couldn't get more zorkmids in the general store.

3rd, and probably even stupider, considering I was doing PR, I didn't
buy a leash in the tool store.  I mean, it's what, 10 zk?  I should
have gotten it.  I'm just so used to pets being all powerful.

4th, I should have watched the pet more carefully around the watch - I
knew it was badly wounded after I rescued it from the watch earlier,
but I let it out of my sight...

So I'm sitting in the general store, selling loot, and I have a sad
feeling...  Oh, shnikies.

RECOVERY:

I had about 1100 zk in cash (some of it halfway across the map), and
lots of loot.  After lots of careful trekking, it turned out that I
had enough cash (after selling all my rings - something I would *NOT*
do except for the PR challenge) for 4 hits of divine protection; I got
3 on the 1st, and a total of 6.  Elbereth is my friend.  Then, thanks
to two high level spellbooks I found, I had enough loot left lying
around minetown to get that 7th point.  I was not about to go petless
hunting for gold with my pickax, challenge or no.

AFTERMATH:

So, this attempt at the PR was a success...but only because I got
lucky after some stupid mistakes.  I won't repeat them next time :)
So, we'll see if I can make 13 ascensions in a row!  Knock on green
#.  I found a new pet, leveled it up some, got my rings out of hock,
and am ready to go on!

So far I've got Mal-Cha-Hum-Wizard, Fem-Neu-Hum-Wizard, Fem-Law-Dwa-
Arc, and now I'm on Mal-Cha-Orc-Bar; if nothing else, I'll have a wide
variety of PR successes :)

Oh, and my new pet ate a chameleon corpse - my orcish barbarian now
has a pet warg :-D

